{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":31620,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"069f0ca8-6504-4f7a-914e-53ba98dfc27f","total_cost_usd":0.23481550000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16931,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":2026,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16931,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16931},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6262,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0063620000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":2026,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16931,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22845350000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"agent\":\"postmortem-writer\",\"screens\":[{\"id\":\"landed\",\"title\":\"LANDED\",\"cause\":\"The ship is on the ground, staged, and you are aboard. The run is over and the haul sells itself, net of the tow fee if you came down away from the yard.\",\"rule_broken\":\"A run ends when the ship is staged, grounded, and crewed — all three. An uncrewed ship on the ground is a non-event; the run keeps going until the astronaut boards it or touches terrain on foot.\",\"armstrong\":\"Down, staged, and you in the seat. That's how it's done, kid — go spend it.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7a\",\"2.3\",\"3b\"]},{\"id\":\"refused\",\"title\":\"REFUSED\",\"cause\":\"The module reached the ground in scrap state. Armstrong would not take delivery of it.\",\"rule_broken\":\"A module delivered in scrap state resolves to refused — a loss, never a win. Scrap never wins, no matter how clean the landing was.\",\"armstrong\":\"I asked for my module back, kid. That ain't it.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7a\",\"2.6c\",\"1b\"]},{\"id\":\"zero_hp\",\"title\":\"0 HP\",\"cause\":\"The ship came apart — hit the ground too fast, or rode the heat bar pinned at capacity long enough to burn through plate, then cargo, then hull.\",\"rule_broken\":\"Heat eats the shield plate first, cargo second, hull last, and only then does the ship die. Landings are graded on vertical speed and no single touchdown can destroy the ship from above the capped hull fraction — so a hard landing that killed her was already a damaged ship.\",\"armstrong\":\"She's scattered across half the yard, kid. Slower next time, or cooler. Pick one.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7a\",\"2.2g\",\"2.3\"]},{\"id\":\"burned_up\",\"title\":\"BURNED UP\",\"cause\":\"You were outside the ship, in atmosphere, above the heat-speed threshold. The suit has no heat protection.\",\"rule_broken\":\"The suit carries no shield. Crossing the interface is only fatal above the heat-speed threshold — but above it, fuel is no defense and the enter key is inert once the heat builds.\",\"armstrong\":\"Suit's got no plate on it, kid. Never had. Be inside her before she starts glowing.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7a\",\"2.4c\",\"1b\"]},{\"id\":\"stranded\",\"title\":\"STRANDED\",\"cause\":\"The run can no longer reach a landing, and there is no input left that would recover it.\",\"rule_broken\":\"One unwinnability check fires when no recovery input remains, and warp shuts off the instant it arms — an unwinnable run is called immediately rather than flown out in real time.\",\"armstrong\":\"Nothing left up there to fly with, kid. Sit tight, drones'll fetch you.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7b\",\"1b\",\"2.1\"]},{\"id\":\"stranded_a\",\"title\":\"STRANDED\",\"cause\":\"The ship cannot deorbit — out of fuel, or staged so the tank is gone — and the arc's periapsis never enters the atmosphere.\",\"rule_broken\":\"Staging is one-way and takes the tank with it. Without thrust, an arc that never dips into the air never comes down. A staged ship on a braking pass is a different animal — an aerobraking orbit already has its periapsis inside the atmosphere, so that one lands.\",\"armstrong\":\"You're circling forever up there, kid. Burn to come home, or don't drop the tank until you can.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7b\",\"2.1\",\"4.5\"]},{\"id\":\"stranded_b\",\"title\":\"STRANDED\",\"cause\":\"The jetpack is dry and you are beyond tether reach of the ship.\",\"rule_broken\":\"The magnet grips the hull too — inside tether range a dry jetpack is an inconvenience, not a loss. Outside it, there is nothing to winch against. Towed mass scales your acceleration inversely, so a piece on the leash narrows that margin fast, and release is always the first remedy.\",\"armstrong\":\"Should've dropped the piece and shot the hull, kid. She was right there.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7b\",\"2.4b\",\"2.4a\"]},{\"id\":\"stranded_c\",\"title\":\"STRANDED\",\"cause\":\"You touched down on the terrain on foot, not aboard the ship.\",\"rule_broken\":\"Landed requires the astronaut aboard — no run ends with the pilot outside. An astronaut touching terrain while not aboard is stranded, and a slow fall through the interface below the heat-speed threshold is survivable, so this is how a gentle descent ends.\",\"armstrong\":\"You walked home, kid. Ship's the part that comes home.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7a\",\"2.4c\",\"3b\"]},{\"id\":\"stranded_d\",\"title\":\"STRANDED\",\"cause\":\"The ship is staged, the chute is shredded, and the best touchdown speed still available is past the destruction cap. The end was already fixed, so it was called here.\",\"rule_broken\":\"A parachute deployed during plasma shreds — the chute waits until the plasma clears and the CHUTE lamp turns green. Without a canopy there is no way left to shed enough speed, and a conservative closed-form check resolves the descent immediately as 0 HP rather than flying it down.\",\"armstrong\":\"Chute stays packed while she's glowing, kid.\",\"grounded_in\":[\"2.7b\",\"2.2f\",\"2.2g\"]}],\"notes\":[\"stranded (the general case) and its four lettered detectors were all given as separate states, so each is written once as required; the general screen names the unwinnability check itself while a–d name their specific detector.\",\"landed is the non-failure state — written as a run ending, not a death, with the ending rule (staged + grounded + crewed) as its teaching line.\",\"zero_hp covers two detectors, hard landing and reentering too hot; both are named in cause and both rules cited are stated in 2.2g/2.3.\",\"stranded_d's armstrong line reuses the canon §1 bark verbatim because the shredded chute is exactly its firing condition; if a canon line may not be reused on a post-mortem screen, substitute a fresh line.\"]}","ttft_ms":30847,"ttft_stream_ms":2296,"time_to_request_ms":707,"type":"result","duration_ms":30914,"uuid":"abf76c79-5f83-42e1-a3fd-815f5e1a92b6"}
